    "lawCode": "Amd §§89-g & 604, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6671\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nauthorizing a thirty year retirement benefit for certain members in\nNassau county\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would modify the service retirement benefit those members of\nthe Employees Retirement System who are employed by Nassau County in a\ncorrection officer title. This bill allows such members to receive an\nadditional pension benefit upon completion of thirty years of service.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISION:\n\nSection 1 - Subdivisions c, g and h of section 89-g of the retirement\nand social security law, as added by chapter 653 of the laws of 1988\nsuch section as renumbered by chapter 771 of the laws of 1988, which\nseeks to ensure Nassau County Correction Officers to obtain a 30 year\nretirement\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, members of the retirement system employed by Nassau County\nwithin a correction officer title do not receive additional service\nretirement benefits for service rendered beyond twenty-five years.\nRetention of experienced correction officers remains an important tool\nfor the safe and orderly functioning of Nassau County's local correc-\ntional facility. Allowing members of the correction officer titles to\nattain additional service retirement benefits serves the dual purpose of\nallowing the county to retain needed, experienced correction officer\npersonnel, as well as rewarding such officers for their additional\nservice to the county beyond their eligibility for retirement.\n\n \nFISCAL:\n\nPlease see fiscal note\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
